#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""kith-ask — ask a kith agent and get its answer back, as a conversation you can continue.

  kith ask <agent> [options] "task"     run the agent on the task in this directory; print its answer
  kith ask <agent> -p ID "task"         ... in project ID's folder on this Mac (project-id --where), from anywhere
  kith ask <agent> -C DIR "task"        ... in DIR
  kith ask <agent> -c "follow-up"       continue the last conversation with that agent from this directory
  kith ask ls                           the conversations kept, newest first
  kith ask <agent>@<machine> "task"     an agent on another machine of yours, over ssh; the owner's runs only (kith remote --help)
  kith ask --bg <agent> [options] "task"  the same run in the background: prints an id at once and returns
  kith ask --to ID "message"            a follow-up to the --bg run ID: queued for its session (kith-wake) and delivered
                                      when its turn ends, or now if it has ended; messages sent before then arrive as
                                      one turn. Prints queued, merged or duplicate (the same message again)
  kith ask --wait ID [--timeout S]      the answers to ID since you last looked (`kith-send --to ask:ID`; waits up to
                                      S seconds, default 600, for the first; exit 3 when none came). For a --bg run:
                                      waits for the run to end, prints its answer and exits with its exit code (every
                                      call prints it again), then what each turn its --to messages woke said
  kith ask --answer ID [--as AGENT] -- TEXT   hand TEXT to whoever asked ID: their answers while they still wait,
                                      else a wake of their session (the host, for a parked card's later turn or no)
  kith ask --answer ID --progress -- TEXT   a progress note instead: kept for --wait (and carried by the answer's wake),
                                      it never wakes anyone. `kith-send --to ask:ID --progress TEXT` does the same
  kith ask --end [--session S]... [--person P]...   Stop, revoke, removal: ends the delegations those sessions or people
                                      started (their --bg runs stopped, their records settled `stopped`, no answer wakes the
                                      caller after), and withdraws the wakes and waiters those callers are owed
  kith ask --sweep                      answers nobody read whose asker's session has ended become its wake (the tick)
  kith ask delegations --json           the delegation records on this Mac, newest first (the host reads them)
  kith ask --cap [N|none]               the cost cap of a delegation chain in dollars (default 5; settings.json
                                      delegation.chain_cost_cap_usd): shows it, or sets it for this Mac

Options: -c/--continue, --as NAME (a named conversation: -c --as NAME picks it up from anywhere, in its folder),
-C/--dir DIR (work in DIR), -p PROJECT (its memory, and its folder unless -C says; the current one if it has none),
-m MODEL, -e EFFORT, -H HARNESS (claude, codex, pi, agy, hermes, qwen, dsh, opencode; default the agent's own),
--json (the whole result: answer, session, cost, turns).

The same run as `kith <agent> "task"`: its pinned package, own settings and services, memory and project, tagged
via=ask in the cost ledger. The difference is what comes back: the answer alone on stdout (status and errors on
stderr, exit 1 when the agent failed), and its session kept so `-c` resumes it with everything it saw and did.
That makes it the way for a script, another harness or a Claude Code session to work with a specialist over
several turns, in the agent's own tools instead of the caller's.

Permission mode: KITH_ASK_PERMISSION_MODE when set, else the agent's settings.json defaultMode, else kith's default (auto;
~/.kith/settings.json changes it). A tool that needs approval asks through a card in the apps, the same as any
one-shot run: the owner answers it (or a member, for their own run's files). A yes within the window (90 s by default)
lets the run go on; later, the run is told to end its turn and kith ask exits 3 with the call's id (`--json`:
`waiting: true`): that is not an answer. The card says "<agent>, asked by <caller>". A yes resumes the agent's session
and what it then says is the id's answer, as is a no or an expiry: `kith ask --wait ID` returns it while the caller's
session is still open; once that session has ended, the answer wakes it instead (kith-wake), exactly once either way
(designs/2026-10-25-access-arch.md M8). The owner's runs for now: a person's run has no ask id. With no host running
there is no card and the tool is refused.
Without --bg the call blocks until the agent has finished (minutes for a real job). With --bg it returns an id at
once: the run goes on detached, its answer and errors are kept in ~/.kith/ask-bg/, and `kith ask --wait ID` collects
them. Everything else (-c, -p, --json, ...) means the same.

Follow-ups: a --bg run notes its session (ID.json, ID.sid) as soon as it holds it, so `kith ask --to ID` can reach it.
The message is a wake of that session (kith-wake, door run: the only way a turn is added to it), so it never types into
a running turn and never starts another conversation: a job with no session to send to says so. A woken turn runs as
the person the job serves, whoever sent it; the owner may send to any job, a person only to their own. `-c` while
the conversation it continues is still running does the same instead of being refused.

Conversations: ~/.kith/ask.json (agent + directory, or --as NAME → session id). A conversation belongs to the
directory it ran in, so after -C or -p, `-c` from inside that folder (or with the same -C/-p) continues it.
Answers: ~/.kith/live/ask/ID.jsonl (ID.read: how many the caller has had), ID.parked while the run waits on a card.
A row is an answer or a progress note (kind): only an answer wakes the caller, once; notes wait in the mailbox.
Delegation record: ID.reg, one per ask id (foreground, --bg, agent@machine), made as the ask begins. It holds who asked
(agent, person), reply_to (the caller's session and ask: the one place the answer's address lives), the chain (the root
ask's id, inherited by asks a run makes through KITH_ASK_ID, or handed to another Mac), the hop (0 at the root), whether
it crossed Macs, its cost, its state (open, answered, capped, stopped) and times. A chain may go 8 asks deep on one Mac
and cross to another at most twice, and may cost US$5 (kith ask --cap): an ask past a cap is refused, exit 4, with
"ask the user before starting another chain"; asks already running finish, and the host raises one Needs-you card when
the cap is reached (without a host the refusal alone says so). A registration from before the record reads as a root ask
at hop 0 with its cost unknown. One lock (.lock) over reading, appending, the records and handing over.
"""
import datetime as dt, fcntl, hashlib, importlib.util, json, os, re, signal, subprocess, sys, time
from contextlib import contextmanager
from importlib.machinery import SourceFileLoader
from pathlib import Path

KITH = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent
sys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)), '..', 'lib'))
from kith_paths import guest_sandbox, paths  # noqa: E402  the one place that knows where kith's folders are
import kith_settings  # noqa: E402  the chain cost cap
KEPT = paths()['KITH_MACHINE'] / 'ask.json'
BG = paths()['KITH_MACHINE'] / 'ask-bg'
BOX = paths()['KITH_MACHINE'] / 'live' / 'ask'
EFFORTS = ('low', 'medium', 'high', 'xhigh', 'max')
ID = re.compile(r'[A-Za-z0-9._-]{1,64}')
KEEP_DAYS = 31   # a delegation record outlives the longest card (cards.expiry_hours, at most 720 h) and its chain's cost
BRIEF_MAX = 2000     # characters of an ask's text a delegation record keeps
MAX_LOCAL_HOPS = 8   # asks deep in a chain on one Mac (as the host's bot requests: serve/host/src/chat/team/requests.rs)
MAX_CROSS_HOPS = 2   # asks in a chain that cross to another Mac
REFUSED = 4          # exit code of an ask a cap refused: not the agent failing, and not "still waiting" (3)


def load():
    try:
        return json.loads(KEPT.read_text())
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return {}


def keep(key, value):
    KEPT.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    with open(KEPT.with_suffix('.lock'), 'w') as lock:
        fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
        kept = load()
        kept[key] = value
        tmp = KEPT.with_suffix('.tmp')
        tmp.write_text(json.dumps(kept, indent=1))
        tmp.replace(KEPT)


def ls():
    kept = sorted(load().items(), key=lambda kv: kv[1].get('at', ''), reverse=True)
    if not kept:
        print('no conversations yet: kith ask <agent> "task"')
    home = str(Path.home())
    for key, v in kept:
        print('%s  %-10s %3d turn(s)  $%-6.2f %s' % (v.get('at', '?'), v.get('agent', '?'), v.get('turns', 0),
                                                   v.get('cost', 0), key.split('|', 1)[1].replace(home, '~', 1)))
        print('    %s' % v.get('last', '')[:110])


def new_id(kind):
    return '%s-%s-%s' % (kind, dt.datetime.now().strftime('%Y%m%d%H%M%S'), os.urandom(3).hex())


@contextmanager
def box_locked():
    """Reading, appending and handing over an id's answers, as one step (M8): kith-wake's lock is only ever taken inside it."""
    BOX.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    with open(BOX / '.lock', 'w') as lock:
        fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
        yield


def box(mid, ext):
    return BOX / ('%s.%s' % (mid, ext))


def upgrade(mid, raw):
    """A delegation record as the code below reads it. A registration made before the record existed has no chain, hop or
    cost: it reads as a root ask at hop 0 with its cost unknown, and keeps working with --wait, --to and --sweep."""
    reg = dict(raw)
    session = reg.pop('session', None)   # the caller's session now lives in reply_to, and only there
    if not isinstance(reg.get('reply_to'), dict):
        reg['reply_to'] = {'session': session, 'ask': None}
    reg.setdefault('chain', mid)
    for key in ('hop', 'cross_hops'):
        reg.setdefault(key, 0)
    reg.setdefault('crossed', False)
    reg.setdefault('cost', None)
    reg.setdefault('state', 'answered' if reg.get('done') else 'open')
    return reg


def read_reg(mid):
    try:
        reg = json.loads(box(mid, 'reg').read_text())
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return None
    return upgrade(mid, reg) if isinstance(reg, dict) else None


def write_reg(mid, reg):
    """Under box_locked: the record, replaced whole and atomically."""
    BOX.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    tmp = box(mid, 'reg.tmp')
    tmp.write_text(json.dumps(reg))
    tmp.replace(box(mid, 'reg'))


def patch_reg(mid, **changes):
    """Under box_locked: change fields of mid's record; nothing when it has none."""
    reg = read_reg(mid)
    if reg is not None:
        reg.update(changes)
        write_reg(mid, reg)
    return reg


def records():
    """Under box_locked: {ask id: record} of every delegation record on this Mac."""
    out = {}
    for f in sorted(BOX.glob('*.reg')) if BOX.is_dir() else ():
        reg = read_reg(f.name[:-len('.reg')])
        if reg:
            out[f.name[:-len('.reg')]] = reg
    return out


def chain_costs(recs):
    """{chain: US$ it has cost}: what a Mac it crossed from had spent when it came here (the most any record says), plus
    the runs of its records here (a record from before costs were kept counts nothing). One pass over recs."""
    base, total = {}, {}
    for r in recs.values():
        base[r['chain']] = max(base.get(r['chain'], 0), r.get('cost_base') or 0)
        total[r['chain']] = total.get(r['chain'], 0) + (r.get('cost') or 0)
    return {c: base[c] + total[c] for c in base}


def refuse(why):
    print('kith ask: %s' % why, file=sys.stderr)
    sys.exit(REFUSED)


def lineage(crossing):
    """Where the ask being made now sits in its chain: the ask whose run is making it (KITH_ASK_ID, which only a run kith
    ask started has) gives the chain and the hop. A run on another Mac that asked across is handed them in KITH_ASK_*.
    Anything else starts a chain, at hop 0."""
    mine = os.environ.get('KITH_ASK_ID') or ''
    parent = read_reg(mine) if ID.fullmatch(mine) else None
    if parent:
        return dict(chain=parent['chain'], hop=parent['hop'] + 1, cross_hops=parent['cross_hops'] + (1 if crossing else 0),
                    ask=mine, cost_base=0, crossed=bool(crossing))
    chain = os.environ.get('KITH_ASK_CHAIN') or ''
    if ID.fullmatch(chain):   # the sender's own record is this hop: it is not counted twice
        try:
            hop, cross = int(os.environ.get('KITH_ASK_HOP') or 0), int(os.environ.get('KITH_ASK_CROSS') or 1)
            base = float(os.environ.get('KITH_ASK_COST') or 0)
        except ValueError:
            refuse('delegation: the chain handed to this ask is not numbers')
        # A chain from another Mac is only as good as its numbers: nothing negative, nothing that skips a cap.
        if not (0 <= hop <= 64 and 0 <= cross <= 64 and 0 <= base < 1e9):   # NaN fails every comparison
            refuse('delegation: the chain handed to this ask has impossible hop or cost numbers')
        return dict(chain=chain, hop=hop, cross_hops=cross, cost_base=base, crossed=True,
                    ask=os.environ.get('KITH_ASK_FROM') or None)
    return dict(chain=None, hop=0, cross_hops=1 if crossing else 0, ask=None, cost_base=0, crossed=bool(crossing))


def open_record(mid, asked, crossing=False, brief=None):
    """The delegation record of ask mid, made as the ask begins and under the box lock (M8): who asked, the address of the
    answer (reply_to: the caller's session and ask, and nowhere else), its chain and hop. Refuses (exit 4) an ask that
    would take its chain over the hop caps or past its cost cap. The caller's wait registration is this same file."""
    with box_locked():
        place = lineage(crossing)
        chain = place['chain'] or mid
        if place['cross_hops'] > MAX_CROSS_HOPS:
            refuse('delegation hop limit: this chain has already crossed to another Mac %d times (at most %d); ask the '
                   'user before starting another chain' % (MAX_CROSS_HOPS, MAX_CROSS_HOPS))
        if max(0, place['hop'] - place['cross_hops']) > MAX_LOCAL_HOPS:
            refuse('delegation hop limit: this chain is already %d asks deep on this Mac (at most %d); ask the user '
                   'before starting another chain' % (MAX_LOCAL_HOPS, MAX_LOCAL_HOPS))
        cap = kith_settings.chain_cost_cap()
        # A chain that came back to this Mac already counts here what it carried: the larger, not the sum.
        spent = max(place['cost_base'], chain_costs(records()).get(chain, 0)) if place['chain'] else 0
        if place['chain'] and cap is not None and spent >= cap:
            refuse('delegation cost cap: chain %s has spent US$%.2f of its US$%g cap; ask the user before starting '
                   'another ask' % (chain, spent, cap))
        reg = {'asked': asked, 'agent': os.environ.get('KITH_AGENT') or None, 'person': os.environ.get('KITH_PERSON') or None,
               'via': os.environ.get('KITH_VIA') or 'terminal',
               'reply_to': {'session': os.environ.get('CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID') or None, 'ask': place['ask']},
               'chain': chain, 'hop': place['hop'], 'cross_hops': place['cross_hops'], 'crossed': place['crossed'],
               'cost': 0.0, 'cost_base': place['cost_base'], 'state': 'open', 'at': time.time(), 'pid': os.getpid(), 'pid_at': time.time()}
        if brief:
            reg['brief'] = brief[:BRIEF_MAX]   # what was asked, for the owner's peek (host only; never in a member's reply)
        write_reg(mid, reg)
        return reg


def sync_state(mid):
    """Under box_locked: an id with an answer in its mailbox is answered (kith-send --to ask:ID writes without telling us)."""
    reg = read_reg(mid)
    if reg and reg['state'] == 'open' and any(kind_of(r) == 'answer' for r in lines_of(mid)):
        patch_reg(mid, state='answered', answered_at=time.time())


def settle(mid, cost, state=None):
    """The run behind mid ended a turn at cost US$: it joins its chain's cost, and a chain that reaches its cap with this
    turn is marked (capped_at, once per cap: the host raises one Needs-you card for it). state: answered, or stopped when
    the run gave no answer; None while it still waits on a card. Runs already going finish; new asks are refused."""
    with box_locked():
        reg = read_reg(mid)
        if not reg:
            return
        reg['cost'] = round((reg.get('cost') or 0) + (cost or 0), 6)
        write_reg(mid, reg)
        cap = kith_settings.chain_cost_cap()
        recs = records()
        tipped = cap is not None and chain_costs(recs).get(reg['chain'], 0) >= cap and \
            not any((r.get('cap_usd') or 0) >= cap for r in recs.values() if r['chain'] == reg['chain'] and r.get('capped_at'))
        if tipped:   # a new cap reached is a new card: the old one's mark does not stand for it
            reg.update(capped_at=time.time(), cap_usd=cap, cap_card_at=None)
        if state and reg['state'] == 'open':
            reg.update(state='capped' if tipped else state, answered_at=time.time())
        if tipped or state:
            write_reg(mid, reg)


def cap_told(chain):
    """kith ask --cap-told CHAIN: the host raised the chain's cap card; it is not raised again for this cap."""
    with box_locked():
        for mid, reg in records().items():
            if reg['chain'] == chain and reg.get('capped_at'):
                patch_reg(mid, cap_card_at=time.time())


def delegation_of(mid):
    """What kith-remote hands the other Mac so its run continues this chain (lineage reads it as KITH_ASK_*): the chain,
    this record's hop and cross hops, the record to answer, and the chain's cost so far."""
    with box_locked():
        reg = read_reg(mid)
        if not reg:
            return None
        return {'chain': reg['chain'], 'hop': reg['hop'], 'cross': reg['cross_hops'], 'from': mid,
                'cost': round(chain_costs(records()).get(reg['chain'], 0), 6)}


def view(mid, reg, costs, cap):
    """A record as the host reads it (serve/contract/kernel/contract.json, Delegation): times in ms, money in
    micro-dollars, a cost that was never kept as null."""
    def ms(t):
        return int(t * 1000) if t else None

    def micro(usd):
        return None if usd is None else int(round(usd * 1e6))
    return {'id': mid, 'agent': reg.get('asked') or '', 'chain': reg['chain'], 'hop': reg['hop'],
            'cross_hops': reg['cross_hops'], 'crossed': bool(reg['crossed']),
            'caller': {'agent': reg.get('agent'), 'person': reg.get('person'), 'via': reg.get('via')},
            'reply_to': {'session': reg['reply_to'].get('session'), 'ask': reg['reply_to'].get('ask')},
            'state': reg['state'], 'cost_micro_usd': micro(reg['cost']),
            'chain_cost_micro_usd': micro(costs.get(reg['chain'], 0)), 'cap_micro_usd': micro(cap),
            'started_ms': ms(reg.get('at')) or 0, 'answered_ms': ms(reg.get('answered_at')),
            'capped_ms': ms(reg.get('capped_at')), 'cap_card_ms': ms(reg.get('cap_card_at')),
            'brief': reg.get('brief') or None, 'session': job_sid(mid)}


def job_sid(mid):
    """The asked agent's session of --bg run mid, once it claimed one (ask-bg/ID.sid); None for any other ask."""
    try:
        return (BG / (mid + '.sid')).read_text().strip() or None
    except OSError:
        return None


def delegations():
    """kith ask delegations --json: every delegation record on this Mac, newest first."""
    with box_locked():
        recs = records()
        costs, cap = chain_costs(recs), kith_settings.chain_cost_cap()
        rows = [view(mid, reg, costs, cap) for mid, reg in recs.items()]
    rows.sort(key=lambda r: r['started_ms'], reverse=True)
    print(json.dumps({'delegations': rows}, ensure_ascii=False))
    return 0


def wake_queue():
    loader = SourceFileLoader('kith_wake', str(KITH / 'bin/kith-wake'))
    mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(importlib.util.spec_from_loader('kith_wake', loader))
    loader.exec_module(mod)
    return mod


def lines_of(mid):
    log = box(mid, 'jsonl')
    return log.read_text().splitlines() if log.exists() else []


def read_count(mid):
    try:
        return int(box(mid, 'read').read_text() or 0)
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return 0


def kind_of(row):
    """progress or answer (the default: a row from before kinds, or from kith-send, is an answer)."""
    try:
        return 'progress' if json.loads(row).get('kind') == 'progress' else 'answer'
    except (ValueError, AttributeError):
        return 'answer'


def said(row):
    try:
        item = json.loads(row)
    except ValueError:
        return None
    return item.get('text') or 'files: ' + ', '.join(item.get('files', [])) + \
        (' (%s)' % item['caption'] if item.get('caption') else '')


def hand_over(mid, wake=None):
    """Under box_locked: once an answer to mid is in, what nobody has read of its mailbox (the progress before it, and
    the answer) goes to the caller's session as a wake when that session has ended (no writer holds it), and counts as
    read. A mailbox with progress only wakes no one. While the session is open they stay here for `--wait`. One wake id
    per row, so a crash between the wake and the count sends nothing twice (kith-wake rule 13)."""
    sync_state(mid)
    reg = read_reg(mid)
    session = (reg or {}).get('reply_to', {}).get('session')
    if not reg or reg.get('delivered') or reg.get('woke_answer') or reg.get('ended_at') or not (session and reg.get('agent')):
        # ended_at: Stop, a revoke or a removal ended it, so no answer wakes the caller after (R8); woke_answer: the answer
        # woke its caller already, later ones are for --wait only
        return 'kept'
    wake = wake or wake_queue()
    if wake.writer_live(session):
        return 'kept'
    rows, done = lines_of(mid), read_count(mid)
    last = max([i for i in range(done, len(rows)) if kind_of(rows[i]) == 'answer'], default=None)
    if last is None:
        return 'kept'
    person = reg.get('person')
    door = 'run' if not person and reg.get('via') in wake.RUN_VIAS else 'host'
    for n in range(done + 1, last + 2):
        row = rows[n - 1]
        text = said(row)
        if text is None:
            continue
        who = (json.loads(row).get('as') or reg.get('asked') or 'the agent')
        progress = kind_of(row) == 'progress'
        try:
            wake.enqueue(session, 'ask:%s/%d' % (mid, n), reg['agent'], ('(progress) ' if progress else '') + text,
                         person=person, door=door,
                         why='%s %s your kith ask %s' % (who, 'reported on' if progress else 'answered', mid))
        except SystemExit as e:
            print('kith ask: %s stays unread: %s' % (mid, e), file=sys.stderr)
            return 'kept'
    box(mid, 'read').write_text(str(last + 1))
    patch_reg(mid, woke_answer=True)
    return 'woke'


def answer(mid, text, who, kind='answer'):
    """kith ask --answer: one reply to mid, appended and handed over in the same step. The same answer again is a
    duplicate and wakes no one twice; a progress reply is stored and wakes no one."""
    with box_locked():
        if (read_reg(mid) or {}).get('ended_at'):
            return 'stopped'   # Stop wins over an answer on its way (R8): nothing is kept, nothing wakes
        if kind == 'answer' and any(kind_of(r) == 'answer' and said(r) == text for r in lines_of(mid)):
            return 'duplicate'
        with open(box(mid, 'jsonl'), 'a') as f:
            f.write(json.dumps({'as': who, 'text': text, 'kind': kind, 'at': dt.datetime.now().isoformat(timespec='seconds')},
                               ensure_ascii=False) + '\n')
        return hand_over(mid)


def finished(mid):
    """The asked run ended without a card open: no answer comes after this one."""
    with box_locked():
        patch_reg(mid, done=True)


def sweep():
    """CallerLeave (M8): every record whose caller's session ended with answers unread wakes it. A record older than
    KEEP_DAYS is forgotten (its answers stay); until then its cost counts towards its chain's cap."""
    out = {}
    if not BOX.is_dir():
        return out
    with box_locked():
        wake = None
        for reg_file in sorted(BOX.glob('*.reg')):
            mid = reg_file.name[:-len('.reg')]
            reg = read_reg(mid) or {}
            if len(lines_of(mid)) > read_count(mid) and not (reg.get('delivered') or reg.get('woke_answer') or reg.get('ended_at')):
                wake = wake or wake_queue()   # loaded once, and only when some mailbox has something unread
                out[mid] = hand_over(mid, wake)
            else:
                out[mid] = 'kept'
            if time.time() - reg.get('at', 0) > KEEP_DAYS * 86400:
                reg_file.unlink(missing_ok=True)
                box(mid, 'parked').unlink(missing_ok=True)
    return out


def claim_pid(mid):
    """A --bg call made the record and returned: the detached run's process is the one an end stops."""
    with box_locked():
        if (read_reg(mid) or {}).get('ended_at'):   # an end came between the record and this claim: the run must not start
            sys.exit(0)
        patch_reg(mid, pid=os.getpid(), pid_at=time.time())


def started_before(pid, t):
    """Whether pid is a live process that began no later than t: a pid recorded at t and reused since began after it."""
    try:
        out = subprocess.run(['ps', '-o', 'etime=', '-p', str(int(pid))], capture_output=True, text=True).stdout.strip()
        days, _, clock = out.rpartition('-')
        parts = [int(x) for x in clock.split(':')]
        secs = sum(n * m for n, m in zip(reversed(parts), (1, 60, 3600))) + (int(days) * 86400 if days else 0)
    except (OSError, ValueError, TypeError):
        return False
    return time.time() - secs <= t + 2


def descendants(pid):
    """pid's children, their children, and so on (one look at the process table)."""
    try:
        table = subprocess.run(['ps', '-A', '-o', 'pid=,ppid='], capture_output=True, text=True).stdout.split('\n')
    except OSError:
        return []
    kids = {}
    for row in table:
        got = row.split()
        if len(got) == 2 and all(x.isdigit() for x in got):
            kids.setdefault(int(got[1]), []).append(int(got[0]))
    out, todo = [], [int(pid)]
    while todo:
        for kid in kids.get(todo.pop(), ()):
            if kid not in out:
                out.append(kid)
                todo.append(kid)
    return out


def stop_run(mid, reg):
    """Stops the run behind mid if it still goes: the agent and what it started (the children of the kith ask process that
    waits for it), then that process. Its pid is checked first, so a reused pid is left alone."""
    pid = reg.get('pid')
    if not pid or int(pid) == os.getpid() or not started_before(pid, reg.get('pid_at') or reg.get('at') or 0):
        return False
    victims = descendants(pid)[::-1] + [int(pid)]
    for victim in victims:
        try:
            os.kill(victim, signal.SIGTERM)
        except OSError:
            pass
    # SIGTERM can be ignored or take its time: whoever is still there after a short grace is killed, as kith-sessions does.
    deadline = time.time() + 2
    while time.time() < deadline and any(alive(v) for v in victims):
        time.sleep(0.1)
    for victim in victims:
        if alive(victim):
            try:
                os.kill(victim, signal.SIGKILL)
            except OSError:
                pass
    return True


def alive(pid):
    try:
        os.kill(pid, 0)
    except ProcessLookupError:
        return False
    except OSError:
        return True
    return True


def end_asks(sessions=(), persons=()):
    """Stop, revoke and removal in one step (R5, R8): every delegation whose caller is one of `sessions` (reply_to.session) or
    `persons` (the person it was asked for, or the person of the --bg job) ends. Its run is stopped, its record is settled
    `stopped` and marked ended (nothing answers into it, hands over or resumes it afterwards), what its mailbox holds counts
    as read, and a card it parked on has nothing to resume. Then the wakes and waiters those callers are owed are withdrawn
    (a turn already running keeps what it carries: the host's Recheck refuses that one). A record already delivered or
    answered to its caller is history and stays. A record from before reply_to has no session and belongs to no lane, unless
    its caller's person is named. Returns the ids ended."""
    sessions, persons = set(sessions), set(persons)
    ended, owed = [], set(sessions)
    wake = wake_queue()
    with box_locked():
        for mid, reg in sorted(records().items()):
            if reg.get('ended_at') or reg.get('delivered') or reg.get('woke_answer'):
                continue
            job = job_of(mid) or {}
            mine = reg['reply_to'].get('session') in sessions if sessions else False
            mine = mine or (reg.get('person') in persons or job.get('person') in persons if persons else False)
            if not mine:
                continue
            stop_run(mid, reg)
            box(mid, 'parked').unlink(missing_ok=True)
            reg.update(state='stopped', ended_at=time.time(), done=True, answered_at=reg.get('answered_at') or time.time())
            write_reg(mid, reg)
            box(mid, 'read').write_text(str(len(lines_of(mid))))
            ended.append(mid)
            if reg['reply_to'].get('session'):
                owed.add(reg['reply_to']['session'])
            try:   # the --bg run's own session is owed follow-ups (kith ask --to): they end with it
                owed.add(open(BG / (mid + '.sid')).read().strip())
            except OSError:
                pass
    owed.discard('')
    for session in sorted(owed):
        wake.withdraw(session)
    if persons:
        wake.withdraw_person(sorted(persons))
    return ended


def note_job(mid, agent, key):
    """A --bg run as it starts: whose job it is and where, for `kith ask --to`. bin/kith adds the session (ID.sid) once
    it holds the session's writer claim."""
    rec = {'agent': agent, 'key': key, 'dir': os.getcwd(), 'person': os.environ.get('KITH_PERSON') or None,
           'at': time.time()}
    tmp = BG / (mid + '.json.tmp')
    tmp.write_text(json.dumps(rec))
    tmp.replace(BG / (mid + '.json'))


def job_of(mid):
    try:
        job = json.loads((BG / (mid + '.json')).read_text())
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return None
    return job if isinstance(job, dict) else None


def job_session(mid, wait=10):
    """The session of --bg run mid; a run still starting gets a few seconds to claim it."""
    sid, end = BG / (mid + '.sid'), time.time() + wait
    while not sid.exists() and not (BG / (mid + '.exit')).exists() and time.time() < end:
        time.sleep(0.5)
    try:
        return sid.read_text().strip() or None
    except OSError:
        return None


def running_job(key):
    """The --bg run still going on the conversation key (newest first), if one is."""
    if not BG.is_dir():
        return None
    for f in sorted(BG.glob('*.json'), key=lambda f: f.stat().st_mtime, reverse=True):
        mid = f.name[:-len('.json')]
        if not (BG / (mid + '.exit')).exists() and (BG / (mid + '.sid')).exists() and (job_of(mid) or {}).get('key') == key:
            return mid
    return None


def caller_person():
    """Who is sending: a person's id, or None for the owner. A guest's shell that dropped KITH_PERSON is no one."""
    person = os.environ.get('KITH_PERSON') or None
    if not person and guest_sandbox():
        sys.exit('kith ask: this is inside a guest\'s run, which can\'t send as the owner')
    return person


def may_ask(agent):
    """Whether the person this call is for may still ask agent today (kith-auth, as bin/kith checks a run)."""
    via = os.environ.get('KITH_AGENT')
    try:
        r = subprocess.run([str(KITH / 'bin/kith-auth'), 'resolve', agent, *(['--via', via] if via and via != agent else [])],
                           capture_output=True, text=True)
        return bool(json.loads(r.stdout).get('allowed'))
    except (OSError, ValueError, AttributeError):   # no answer is no
        return False


def follow_up(sid, agent, person, rid, text, why):
    """One wake request on sid (kith-wake: merged with what else it is owed, delivered once when nobody holds it)."""
    wake = wake_queue()
    try:
        got = wake.enqueue(sid, rid, agent, text, person=person, door='host' if person else 'run', why=why)
    except SystemExit as e:
        sys.exit('kith ask: %s' % e)
    if got == 'duplicate':
        how = wake.status(rid)[0]
        print('kith ask: that message was sent already (%s)' % {'queued': 'still queued', 'running': 'in the turn now'}
              .get(how, how), file=sys.stderr)
    return got


def send_to(mid, text):
    """kith ask --to ID TEXT: a follow-up to the --bg run ID."""
    if not ID.fullmatch(mid) or not (BG / (mid + '.cmd')).exists():
        sys.exit('kith ask: no job %s on this Mac (kith ask --bg prints the ids)' % mid)
    job, sid = job_of(mid), job_session(mid)
    if not job or not sid:
        sys.exit('kith ask: %s has no session to send to (it ended before it began one, or runs on a harness other than '
                 'claude); ask anew without --to' % mid)
    caller = caller_person()
    if caller is not None and (caller != job.get('person') or not may_ask(job['agent'])):
        sys.exit('kith ask: %s is not one of your jobs' % mid)
    rid = 'ask-to:%s/%s' % (mid, hashlib.sha256(text.encode()).hexdigest()[:12])
    who = os.environ.get('KITH_AGENT') or caller or 'the owner'
    got = follow_up(sid, job['agent'], job.get('person'), rid, text, '%s sent a follow-up to kith ask %s' % (who, mid))
    to = BG / (mid + '.to')
    if rid not in (to.read_text().split() if to.exists() else []):
        with open(to, 'a') as f:
            f.write(rid + '\n')
    if got != 'duplicate':
        when = ('had ended: its session resumes now with your message' if (BG / (mid + '.exit')).exists() else
                'is still running: your message reaches it when its turn ends')
        print('%s %s; follow it: kith ask --wait %s' % (mid, when, mid), file=sys.stderr)
    print(got)
    return 0


def follow_ups(mid, end, code):
    """After a --bg run's own answer: what each turn its --to messages woke said, once per turn, in order."""
    to = BG / (mid + '.to')
    if not to.exists():
        return code
    wake, rids = wake_queue(), to.read_text().split()
    while True:
        got = [wake.status(r) for r in rids]
        if all(how not in ('queued', 'running') for how, _ in got) or time.time() >= end:
            break
        time.sleep(1)
    shown = []
    for how, run in got:
        if how in ('queued', 'running'):
            print('kith ask: a follow-up to %s is still to come; ask again with: kith ask --wait %s' % (mid, mid),
                  file=sys.stderr)
            return 3
        if run and run not in shown:
            shown.append(run)
            for ext, stream in (('log', sys.stdout), ('err', sys.stderr)):
                f = wake.logs_dir() / ('%s.%s' % (run, ext))
                stream.write(f.read_text(errors='replace') if f.exists() else '')
        if how in ('answered', 'recovered'):
            code = 0
        elif how == 'withdrawn':
            print('kith ask: a follow-up to %s was withdrawn before it reached the job' % mid, file=sys.stderr)
        else:
            print('kith ask: a follow-up to %s ended %s' % (mid, how), file=sys.stderr)
            code = 1
    return code


def kick_wakes(sid):
    """The run's turn ended: a wake its session is owed (a --to message) is delivered now, not at the next tick."""
    wake = wake_queue()
    if sid and wake.item_path(sid).exists():
        wake.spawn_drain()


def wait_bg(mid, timeout):
    """The answer of a `kith ask --bg` run: waits for it to end, then prints what it printed."""
    out, err, code = BG / (mid + '.out'), BG / (mid + '.err'), BG / (mid + '.exit')
    end = time.time() + timeout
    while not code.exists() and time.time() < end:
        time.sleep(1)
    if not code.exists():
        print('kith ask: %s is still running; ask again with: kith ask --wait %s' % (mid, mid), file=sys.stderr)
        return 3
    sys.stdout.write(out.read_text() if out.exists() else '')
    sys.stderr.write(err.read_text() if err.exists() else '')
    try:
        return int(code.read_text().strip() or 1)
    except ValueError:
        return 1


def background(argv):
    """Run this same call detached; print its id at once. The wrapper writes the exit code last, atomically."""
    mid = new_id('bg')
    open_record(mid, argv[0], crossing='@' in argv[0], brief=argv[-1] if len(argv) > 1 else None)   # a refused ask says so now, not in a log
    BG.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    (BG / (mid + '.cmd')).write_text(' '.join(argv) + '\n')
    base = str(BG / mid)
    script = '"$@" >"$0.out" 2>"$0.err" </dev/null; echo $? >"$0.exit.tmp"; mv "$0.exit.tmp" "$0.exit"'
    # The run's ask id is the bg id, so a later answer to a card it parks on comes to the same --wait.
    subprocess.Popen(['/bin/sh', '-c', script, base, sys.executable, os.path.abspath(__file__), *argv],
                     stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL,
                     start_new_session=True, env=dict(os.environ, KITH_ASK_BG=mid))
    print('started %s in the background as %s; its answer: kith ask --wait %s' % (argv[0], mid, mid))
    return 0


def wait(argv):
    """kith ask --wait ID [--timeout S]: the answers since last time; the first may take a while."""
    mid = argv[0] if argv else ''
    if not ID.fullmatch(mid):
        sys.exit('usage: kith ask --wait ID [--timeout SECONDS]')
    timeout = float(argv[argv.index('--timeout') + 1]) if '--timeout' in argv else 600
    end = time.time() + timeout
    if (BG / (mid + '.cmd')).exists():
        code = wait_bg(mid, timeout)
        # A --bg run that parked on a card (exit 3, its record not marked delivered) has its answer still to come: below.
        reg = read_reg(mid)
        if not (code == 3 and (BG / (mid + '.exit')).exists() and reg and not reg.get('delivered')):
            return follow_ups(mid, end, code) if (BG / (mid + '.exit')).exists() else code
    def answered():
        return any(kind_of(r) == 'answer' for r in lines_of(mid)[read_count(mid):])
    while not answered() and time.time() < end:
        time.sleep(2)
    with box_locked():   # the sweep may have handed them to a wake meanwhile
        rows, done = lines_of(mid), read_count(mid)
        if len(rows) <= done:
            print('kith ask: no answer to %s yet; ask again with: kith ask --wait %s' % (mid, mid), file=sys.stderr)
            return 3
        for row in rows[done:]:
            text = said(row)
            if text is not None:
                print(('(progress) ' if kind_of(row) == 'progress' else '') + text)
        box(mid, 'read').write_text(str(len(rows)))
        sync_state(mid)
        if not any(kind_of(r) == 'answer' for r in rows[done:]):   # progress is not the answer: still waiting
            print('kith ask: no answer to %s yet; ask again with: kith ask --wait %s' % (mid, mid), file=sys.stderr)
            return 3
    return 0


def answer_cmd(argv):
    """kith ask --answer ID [--as AGENT] [--progress] -- TEXT"""
    usage = 'usage: kith ask --answer ID [--as AGENT] [--progress] -- TEXT'
    if '--' not in argv:
        sys.exit(usage)
    head, text = argv[:argv.index('--')], ' '.join(argv[argv.index('--') + 1:]).strip()
    if not text or not head or not ID.fullmatch(head[0]):
        sys.exit(usage)
    who, kind, i = None, 'answer', 1
    while i < len(head):
        if head[i] == '--as' and i + 1 < len(head): who = head[i + 1]; i += 2
        elif head[i] == '--progress': kind = 'progress'; i += 1
        else: sys.exit(usage)
    print(answer(head[0], text, who, kind))
    return 0


def from_agent_run():
    """Whether this call comes from inside an agent's run: an agent doesn't lift its own caps."""
    return any(os.environ.get(k) for k in ('KITH_ASK_ID', 'KITH_AGENT', 'CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID'))


def cap_cmd(argv):
    """kith ask --cap [N|none]: the cost cap of a delegation chain, US$ (shown, or set for this Mac)."""
    if len(argv) > 1:
        sys.exit('usage: kith ask --cap [N|none]')
    if argv and from_agent_run():
        sys.exit('kith ask: the cap is the owner\'s to change (the Needs-you card, or kith ask --cap in a terminal), '
                 'not an agent\'s')
    if argv:
        try:
            kith_settings.set_chain_cost_cap(argv[0])
        except ValueError as e:
            sys.exit('kith ask: %s' % e)
    cap = kith_settings.chain_cost_cap()
    print('none' if cap is None else '%g' % cap)
    return 0


def reply(argv):
    """kith ask --reply ID AGENT --resume SESSION -- NOTE: the host's resume of a run that parked on a card for the ask ID
    (cards/resume.rs). What the resumed turn says is ID's answer, unless it parks again on another card."""
    if len(argv) < 6 or not ID.fullmatch(argv[0]) or argv[2] != '--resume' or argv[4] != '--':
        sys.exit('usage: kith ask --reply ID AGENT --resume SESSION -- NOTE')
    mid, agent, session, note = argv[0], argv[1], argv[3], ' '.join(argv[5:])
    if (read_reg(mid) or {}).get('ended_at'):   # Stop wins over a yes already given (R8): the run is not resumed
        print('kith ask: %s was ended; nothing to resume' % mid, file=sys.stderr)
        return 0
    box(mid, 'parked').unlink(missing_ok=True)
    env = dict(os.environ, KITH_OUTPUT='json', KITH_LAUNCH_ASK_ID=mid)
    proc = subprocess.run([str(KITH / 'bin/kith'), agent, '--resume', session, '--', note], env=env,
                          stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, capture_output=True, text=True)
    try:
        res = json.loads(proc.stdout)
    except ValueError:   # never started (the session is held, ...): the host tries again, nothing is answered
        sys.stderr.write((proc.stderr or proc.stdout or 'kith ask: %s gave no answer\n' % agent)[-3000:])
        return proc.returncode or 1
    settle(mid, res.get('total_cost_usd'))
    if box(mid, 'parked').exists():
        return 0
    answer(mid, res.get('result') or '%s ended its turn without an answer' % agent, agent)
    finished(mid)
    return 1 if res.get('is_error') else 0


def main(argv):
    if not argv or argv[0] in ('-h', '--help'):
        print(__doc__.strip()); return 0
    # A guest's shell cannot start a run (no network, login or agents folder in its sandbox): the helper its membership
    # grants is asked through a tool that runs outside, as the kith launcher says too.
    if guest_sandbox():
        print('kith ask: from a guest\'s shell a helper is asked with the ask_helper tool '
              '(mcp__kithpermit__ask_helper: agent and task), for a helper your membership grants.', file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    bg = '--bg' in argv   # anywhere before the task's `--`
    if bg:
        argv = [a for a in argv if a != '--bg']
    if argv[0] == 'ls':
        ls(); return 0
    if argv[0] == '--wait':
        return wait(argv[1:])
    if argv[0] == '--to':
        if len(argv) < 3 or not ' '.join(argv[2:]).strip():
            sys.exit('usage: kith ask --to ID "message"')
        return send_to(argv[1], ' '.join(a for a in argv[2:] if a != '--').strip())
    if argv[0] == '--answer':
        return answer_cmd(argv[1:])
    if argv[0] == '--reply':
        return reply(argv[1:])
    if argv[0] == '--cap':
        return cap_cmd(argv[1:])
    if argv[0] == '--cap-told':
        if len(argv) != 2 or not ID.fullmatch(argv[1]):
            sys.exit('usage: kith ask --cap-told CHAIN')
        if from_agent_run():
            sys.exit('kith ask: only the host marks a cap card raised')
        cap_told(argv[1]); return 0
    if argv[0] == '--end':
        if from_agent_run():
            sys.exit('kith ask: only the owner (or the host, on Stop, a revoke or a removal) ends delegations')
        sessions, persons, i = [], [], 1
        while i < len(argv):
            if argv[i] in ('--session', '--person') and i + 1 < len(argv):
                (sessions if argv[i] == '--session' else persons).append(argv[i + 1]); i += 2
            else:
                sys.exit('usage: kith ask --end [--session S]... [--person P]...')
        print('ended %s' % ' '.join(end_asks(sessions, persons)))
        return 0
    if argv[0] == 'delegations':   # --json is the only form
        return delegations()
    if argv[0] == '--sweep':
        for mid, what in sweep().items():
            if what == 'woke':
                print('%s: answers handed to its asker\'s session as a wake' % mid)
        return 0
    if '@' in argv[0]:  # an agent on another machine
        if bg:
            return background(argv)
        # The record is made here (the hop caps and the cost cap apply before anything leaves); kith-remote sends the chain
        # along and settles the record with the other Mac's cost.
        mid = os.environ.pop('KITH_ASK_BG', None) or new_id('ask')
        if read_reg(mid) is None:
            open_record(mid, argv[0], crossing=True)
        else:
            claim_pid(mid)
        code = 1
        try:
            code = subprocess.run([str(KITH / 'bin/kith-remote'), 'ask', *argv],
                                  env=dict(os.environ, KITH_ASK_RECORD=mid)).returncode
        finally:   # kith-remote settles a call it made; an early refusal or a crash must not leave the record open
            if code != 0:
                settle(mid, 0, 'stopped')
        return code
    agent, rest = argv[0], argv[1:]
    cont, name, as_json, where, kith_opts, words, i = False, None, False, None, [], [], 0
    while i < len(rest):
        a = rest[i]
        if a in ('-c', '--continue'): cont = True; i += 1
        elif a == '--as': name = rest[i + 1]; i += 2
        elif a == '--json': as_json = True; i += 1
        elif a in ('-C', '--dir'): where = rest[i + 1]; i += 2
        elif a in ('-p', '--project', '-m', '--model', '-e', '--effort', '-H', '--harness'):
            if a in ('-e', '--effort') and rest[i + 1] not in EFFORTS:
                sys.exit('kith ask: effort must be one of %s' % ', '.join(EFFORTS))
            kith_opts += [a, rest[i + 1]]; i += 2
        elif a == '--': words += rest[i + 1:]; break
        else: words.append(a); i += 1
    task = ' '.join(words).strip()
    if not task:
        sys.exit('usage: kith ask <agent> [-c] [--as NAME] [-C DIR] [-p PROJECT] [-m MODEL] [-e EFFORT] [-H HARNESS] [--json] "task"')
    if bg:   # runs detached, as the call without --bg
        return background([agent, *rest])

    # Where the agent works: -C, else the folder of the project -p names, else a named conversation's own folder.
    project = next((v for f, v in zip(kith_opts[::2], kith_opts[1::2]) if f in ('-p', '--project')), None)
    if not where and project:
        found = subprocess.run([str(KITH / 'bin/project-id'), '--where', project], capture_output=True, text=True)
        where = found.stdout.strip() or None
        if not where and not found.stderr:   # an unknown project: bin/kith says so
            print('kith ask: %s has no folder on this Mac, so %s works here; to give it one: \'%s\' --register %s DIR'
                  % (project, agent, KITH / 'bin/project-id', project), file=sys.stderr)
    if not where and cont and name:
        where = (load().get('%s|as:%s' % (agent, name)) or {}).get('dir')
    started = os.getcwd()
    if where:
        try:
            os.chdir(os.path.expanduser(where))
        except OSError as e:
            sys.exit('kith ask: cannot work in %s: %s' % (where, e.strerror))

    key = '%s|%s' % (agent, ('as:' + name) if name else os.getcwd())
    prev = load().get(key) if cont else None
    # The conversation is still running (a --bg job, or another run holds its session): the message is its next turn.
    running = running_job(key) if cont else None
    if running:
        return send_to(running, task)
    if prev and not os.environ.get('KITH_PERSON') and wake_queue().writer_live(prev['session_id']):
        sid = prev['session_id']
        got = follow_up(sid, agent, None, 'ask-c:%s/%s' % (sid, hashlib.sha256(task.encode()).hexdigest()[:12]), task,
                        '%s continued this conversation while it was running' % (os.environ.get('KITH_AGENT') or 'the owner'))
        if got != 'duplicate':
            print('%s is still answering in that conversation: your message is its next turn' % agent, file=sys.stderr)
        print(got)
        return 0
    if cont and not prev:
        sys.exit('kith ask: no conversation with %s %s to continue; start one without -c'
                 % (agent, 'named ' + name if name else 'from this directory'))

    # A continued conversation keeps its project, model, effort and harness unless this call names new ones.
    given = kith_opts[::2]
    for flag, alias in (('-p', '--project'), ('-m', '--model'), ('-e', '--effort'), ('-H', '--harness')):
        if prev and flag not in given and alias not in given and (prev.get('opts') or {}).get(flag):
            kith_opts += [flag, prev['opts'][flag]]
    opts = {(f if len(f) == 2 else '-' + {'harness': 'H'}.get(f[2:], f[2])): v
            for f, v in zip(kith_opts[::2], kith_opts[1::2])}

    env = dict(os.environ, KITH_VIA='ask', KITH_OUTPUT='json')   # bin/kith: the same for every harness
    # The asked agent's room shows the run as a card, "asked by <caller>" (a terminal when no agent is asking): bin/kith-sessions.
    env.update(KITH_LAUNCH_KIND='ask', KITH_LAUNCH_LABEL=os.environ.get('KITH_AGENT', ''))
    if os.environ.get('KITH_ASK_PERMISSION_MODE'):
        env['KITH_PERMISSION_MODE'] = os.environ['KITH_ASK_PERMISSION_MODE']
    if prev:
        env['KITH_RESUME'] = prev['session_id']
    # This call's id: a card the run parks on answers it later (--bg: the bg id, so the same --wait collects it).
    bg_id = env.pop('KITH_ASK_BG', None)
    mid = bg_id or new_id('ask')
    if bg_id:
        note_job(bg_id, agent, key)
        env['KITH_LAUNCH_SID_FILE'] = str(BG / (bg_id + '.sid'))
    if read_reg(mid) is None:   # a --bg call made it when it began
        open_record(mid, agent, brief=task)
    elif bg_id:
        claim_pid(mid)
    # A run kith-remote started for another Mac's ask got its chain in KITH_ASK_*: the record holds it now, and the run's
    # own asks find it through KITH_ASK_ID.
    for k in ('KITH_ASK_CHAIN', 'KITH_ASK_HOP', 'KITH_ASK_CROSS', 'KITH_ASK_FROM', 'KITH_ASK_COST'):
        env.pop(k, None)
    env['KITH_LAUNCH_ASK_ID'] = mid
    proc = subprocess.run([str(KITH / 'bin/kith'), agent, *kith_opts, '--', task], env=env, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL,
                          capture_output=True, text=True)
    if bg_id:
        kick_wakes(job_session(bg_id, wait=0))
    parked = box(mid, 'parked').exists()
    try:
        res = json.loads(proc.stdout)
    except ValueError:
        settle(mid, 0, None if parked else 'stopped')
        sys.stderr.write((proc.stderr or proc.stdout or 'kith ask: %s gave no answer\n' % agent)[-3000:])
        return proc.returncode or 1
    # Not parked: the answer goes straight back to this call, so nothing is left for a wake. Parked: the card's answer comes.
    settle(mid, res.get('total_cost_usd'), None if parked else ('stopped' if res.get('is_error') else 'answered'))
    if not parked:
        with box_locked():
            patch_reg(mid, done=True, delivered=True)

    sid, text = res.get('session_id'), res.get('result') or ''
    turns = (prev or {}).get('turns', 0) + 1
    cost = (prev or {}).get('cost', 0) + (res.get('total_cost_usd') or 0)
    if sid:
        keep(key, {'agent': agent, 'session_id': sid, 'at': dt.datetime.now().isoformat(timespec='minutes'),
                   'turns': turns, 'cost': round(cost, 4), 'opts': opts, 'dir': os.getcwd(),
                   'last': ' '.join(task.split())})
    if parked:   # not an answer: that comes when the card is answered
        if as_json:
            print(json.dumps({'agent': agent, 'answer': None, 'waiting': True, 'id': mid, 'session_id': sid,
                              'turn': turns, 'cost_usd': res.get('total_cost_usd'), 'num_turns': res.get('num_turns')},
                             ensure_ascii=False))
        else:
            print('%s is waiting on an approval card; its answer: kith ask --wait %s' % (agent, mid))
        return 3
    if as_json:
        print(json.dumps({'agent': agent, 'answer': text, 'session_id': sid, 'error': bool(res.get('is_error')),
                          'turn': turns, 'cost_usd': res.get('total_cost_usd'), 'num_turns': res.get('num_turns')},
                         ensure_ascii=False))
    else:
        print(text)
        moved = '' if name or os.getcwd() == started else (' -p ' + project if project else " -C '%s'" % os.getcwd())
        again = 'kith ask %s -c%s "…"' % (agent, (' --as ' + name) if name else moved)
        print('\n[%s · turn %d · $%.2f this turn · continue: %s]'
              % (agent, turns, res.get('total_cost_usd') or 0, again), file=sys.stderr)
    return 1 if res.get('is_error') else 0


if __name__ == '__main__':
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
